> the wrong place (it might be that the problem is with Eterm and not with
> the font). Do you have any idea what the problem might be and how to fix
> it?

I spent some time figuring this one out a while ago.

The problem is that the character symbol used is considered by xterm to be
an "unprintable character".  On the rogue level, with IBMGraphics, the
symbol used for the character is that "smiley face" char.  I don't remember
the exact char code, but it's somewhere below 32 (space), and so newer
versions of xterm refuse to print it.  (It works for me if I play in the
linux console, by the way, and it worked with an older version of xterm).

Unfortunately, I don't know how to fix the problem.  My work around is
usually to toggle IBMGraphics when I get to this level, although you can
also get around it by riding a steed.

The most helpful advice I got on #nethack was along the lines of "well, you
shouldn't be using this non-standard charset anyway"... :)

